{"id":"mahabharata-12-338","work":"mahabharata","part":12,"partName":"शान्तिपर्व","partNameEn":"Shanti Parva","unit":338,"title":"अष्टात्रिंशदधिकत्रिशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 338 · Rudra asks Brahma about the One","summary":{"en":"Janamejaya asks whether there are many persons or only one, and which is highest, and Vaishampayana tells of Rudra going to Brahma on the Vaijayanta mountain in the milk ocean. Brahma tells Rudra that, as the many persons have one womb, so the one supreme Person is the source of them all.","kn":"ಅನೇಕ ಪುರುಷರಿದ್ದಾರೋ ಒಬ್ಬನೇ ಇದ್ದಾನೋ, ಯಾರು ಶ್ರೇಷ್ಠನೆಂದು ಜನಮೇಜಯ ಕೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ; ಕ್ಷೀರಸಾಗರದ ವೈಜಯಂತ ಪರ್ವತದಲ್ಲಿ ರುದ್ರ ಬ್ರಹ್ಮನ ಬಳಿ ಹೋದುದನ್ನು ವೈಶಂಪಾಯನ ಹೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಅನೇಕ ಪುರುಷರಿಗೆ ಒಂದೇ ಯೋನಿಯಿರುವಂತೆ ಪರಮ ಪುರುಷನೇ ಎಲ್ಲರ ಮೂಲವೆಂದು ಬ್ರಹ್ಮ ಹೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"जनमेजय पूछते हैं कि अनेक पुरुष हैं या एक ही और कौन श्रेष्ठ है, और वैशम्पायन क्षीरसागर के वैजयन्त पर्वत पर रुद्र के ब्रह्मा के पास जाने की कथा कहते हैं। ब्रह्मा बताते हैं कि जैसे अनेक पुरुषों की एक ही योनि है वैसे परम पुरुष ही सबका स्रोत है।","te":"అనేక పురుషులున్నారా లేక ఒక్కడేనా, ఎవరు శ్రేష్ఠుడని జనమేజయుడు అడుగుతాడు; క్షీరసాగరంలోని వైజయంత పర్వతంపై రుద్రుడు బ్రహ్మ వద్దకు వెళ్లిన కథను వైశంపాయనుడు చెబుతాడు. అనేక పురుషులకు ఒకే యోని ఉన్నట్లు పరమ పురుషుడే అందరికీ మూలమని బ్రహ్మ అంటాడు.","ta":"பல புருஷர்கள் உள்ளனரா ஒருவனே உள்ளானா, யார் உயர்ந்தவன் என்று ஜனமேஜயன் கேட்க, பாற்கடலின் வைஜயந்த மலையில் ருத்ரன் பிரம்மனிடம் சென்ற கதையை வைசம்பாயனர் கூறுகிறார். பல புருஷருக்கு ஒரே கருப்பை உள்ளது போல் பரம புருஷனே அனைவருக்கும் மூலம் என்று பிரம்மன் கூறுகிறான்.","ml":"പുരുഷന്മാർ പലരാണോ ഒരാളാണോ, അവരിൽ ഉത്തമനാര് എന്നിവ ജനമേജയൻ ചോദിക്കുന്നു. പാലാഴിയിലെ വൈജയന്തപർവ്വതത്തിൽ ബ്രഹ്മാവിന്റെ അടുത്തെത്തിയ രുദ്രന്റെ കഥ വൈശമ്പായനൻ പറയുന്നു. ഒരേ ഗർഭത്തിൽ പലർ ഉള്ളതുപോലെ, ഏകനായ പരമപുരുഷനാണ് അവരുടെയെല്ലാം ഉറവിടമെന്ന് ബ്രഹ്മാവ് പറയുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 12.338; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Wed Jun 16 2021","sections":[{"title":"मोक्षधर्मपर्व","titleEn":"Mokshadharma Parva (Duties for liberation)","verses":[{"text":"जनमेजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Janamejaya said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"बहवः पुरुषा ब्रह्मन्नुताहो एक एव तु ।\nको ह्यत्र पुरुषः श्रेष्ठः को वा योनिरिहोच्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Brahmin, are there many Persons, or only one? Which Person here is the best, or what is called the source here?"}},{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":2,"text":"बहवः पुरुषा लोके सांख्ययोगविचारिणाम् ।\nनैतदिच्छन्ति पुरुषमेकं कुरुकुलोद्वह ॥","meaning":{"en":"Among those who reflect on Samkhya and yoga, descendant of the Kurus, there are said to be many Persons in the world; they do not accept a single Person."}},{"n":3,"text":"बहूनां पुरुषाणां च यथैका योनिरुच्यते ।\nतथा तं पुरुषं विश्वं व्याख्यास्यामि गुणाधिकम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Just as one source is spoken of for many persons, so I will explain that Person, the universe, surpassing in quality."}},{"n":4,"text":"नमस्कृत्वा तु गुरवे व्यासायामिततेजसे ।\nतपोयुक्ताय दान्ताय वन्द्याय परमर्षये ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having bowed to my teacher Vyasa of boundless splendor, rich in austerity, self-controlled, worthy of homage, the supreme sage,"}},{"n":5,"text":"इदं पुरुषसूक्तं हि सर्ववेदेषु पार्थिव ।\nऋतं सत्यं च विख्यातमृषिसिंहेन चिन्तितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"king, this hymn of the Person, found in all the Vedas, famed as order and truth, was pondered by that lion among sages."}},{"n":6,"text":"उत्सर्गेणापवादेन ऋषिभिः कपिलादिभिः ।\nअध्यात्मचिन्तामाश्रित्य शास्त्राण्युक्तानि भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bharata, the sages Kapila and others, relying on reflection on the self, have spoken the scriptures in both general rule and exception."}},{"n":7,"text":"समासतस्तु यद्व्यासः पुरुषैकत्वमुक्तवान् ।\nतत्तेऽहं संप्रवक्ष्यामि प्रसादादमितौजसः ॥","meaning":{"en":"What Vyasa said in brief of the oneness of the Person, I will tell you, by the grace of that being of boundless might."}},{"n":8,"text":"अत्राप्युदाहरन्तीममितिहासं पुरातनम् ।\nब्रह्मणा सह संवादं त्र्यम्बकस्य विशां पते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Here too they cite this ancient tale, a conversation between Brahma and the Three-eyed one, lord of the people."}},{"n":9,"text":"क्षीरोदस्य समुद्रस्य मध्ये हाटकसप्रभः ।\nवैजयन्त इति ख्यातः पर्वतप्रवरो नृप ॥","meaning":{"en":"In the middle of the Milk Ocean there is a golden-shining, best of mountains, king, famed as Vaijayanta."}},{"n":10,"text":"तत्राध्यात्मगतिं देव एकाकी प्रविचिन्तयन् ।\nवैराजसदने नित्यं वैजयन्तं निषेवते ॥","meaning":{"en":"There the god, alone, contemplating the path of the Self, constantly frequents Vaijayanta, in the abode of Viraj."}},{"n":11,"text":"अथ तत्रासतस्तस्य चतुर्वक्त्रस्य धीमतः ।\nललाटप्रभवः पुत्रः शिव आगाद्यदृच्छया ।\nआकाशेनैव योगीशः पुरा त्रिनयनः प्रभुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"While the wise four-faced Brahma was sitting there, his son born of his forehead, Shiva, the three-eyed lord and master of yogis, came by chance, through the sky itself, as of old."}},{"n":12,"text":"ततः खान्निपपाताशु धरणीधरमूर्धनि ।\nअग्रतश्चाभवत्प्रीतो ववन्दे चापि पादयोः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then he quickly dropped from the sky onto the mountain's summit, stood before him pleased, and bowed at his feet."}},{"n":13,"text":"तं पादयोर्निपतितं दृष्ट्वा सव्येन पाणिना ।\nउत्थापयामास तदा प्रभुरेकः प्रजापतिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing him fallen at his feet, the sole lord of creatures raised him up with his left hand."}},{"n":14,"text":"उवाच चैनं भगवांश्चिरस्यागतमात्मजम् ।\nस्वागतं ते महाबाहो दिष्ट्या प्राप्तोऽसि मेऽन्तिकम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The blessed one said to his son, who had come after a long time: \"Welcome, mighty-armed one; it is fortunate that you have come near me."}},{"n":15,"text":"कच्चित्ते कुशलं पुत्र स्वाध्यायतपसोः सदा ।\nनित्यमुग्रतपास्त्वं हि ततः पृच्छामि ते पुनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Son, are you well in your recitation and austerity? You are always one of fierce austerity, so I ask you again.\""}},{"text":"रुद्र उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Rudra said:"}},{"n":16,"text":"त्वत्प्रसादेन भगवन्स्वाध्यायतपसोर्मम ।\nकुशलं चाव्ययं चैव सर्वस्य जगतस्तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"By your grace, blessed one, my recitation and austerity are well, and so is all the world, unfailing."}},{"n":17,"text":"चिरदृष्टो हि भगवान्वैराजसदने मया ।\nततोऽहं पर्वतं प्राप्तस्त्विमं त्वत्पादसेवितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"I have long seen the blessed one in the abode of Viraj, and so I have come to this mountain served by your feet."}},{"n":18,"text":"कौतूहलं चापि हि मे एकान्तगमनेन ते ।\nनैतत्कारणमल्पं हि भविष्यति पितामह ॥","meaning":{"en":"I am also curious about your going off alone; this cannot be a small reason, grandfather."}},{"n":19,"text":"किं नु तत्सदनं श्रेष्ठं क्षुत्पिपासाविवर्जितम् ।\nसुरासुरैरध्युषितमृषिभिश्चामितप्रभैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"What of that excellent abode, free of hunger and thirst, lived in by gods, asuras, and sages of boundless radiance,"}},{"n":20,"text":"गन्धर्वैरप्सरोभिश्च सततं संनिषेवितम् ।\nउत्सृज्येमं गिरिवरमेकाकी प्राप्तवानसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"always frequented by gandharvas and apsarases? Leaving it, you came alone to this best of mountains."}},{"text":"ब्रह्मोवाच","meaning":{"en":"Brahma said:"}},{"n":21,"text":"वैजयन्तो गिरिवरः सततं सेव्यते मया ।\nअत्रैकाग्रेण मनसा पुरुषश्चिन्त्यते विराट् ॥","meaning":{"en":"I always frequent Vaijayanta, the best of mountains; here, with a one-pointed mind, I contemplate the cosmic Person."}},{"text":"रुद्र उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Rudra said:"}},{"n":22,"text":"बहवः पुरुषा ब्रह्मंस्त्वया सृष्टाः स्वयंभुवा ।\nसृज्यन्ते चापरे ब्रह्मन्स चैकः पुरुषो विराट् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Brahma, you, the self-existent one, have created many Persons, and others are being created; yet there is one Person, the cosmic one."}},{"n":23,"text":"को ह्यसौ चिन्त्यते ब्रह्मंस्त्वया वै पुरुषोत्तमः ।\nएतन्मे संशयं ब्रूहि महत्कौतूहलं हि मे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Who is that Supreme Person you contemplate, Brahma? Tell me this doubt of mine; my curiosity is great."}},{"text":"ब्रह्मोवाच","meaning":{"en":"Brahma said:"}},{"n":24,"text":"बहवः पुरुषाः पुत्र ये त्वया समुदाहृताः ।\nएवमेतदतिक्रान्तं द्रष्टव्यं नैवमित्यपि ।\nआधारं तु प्रवक्ष्यामि एकस्य पुरुषस्य ते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Son, the many Persons you speak of: what you describe has passed, and it should not be seen so. But I will tell you the basis of the one Person."}},{"n":25,"text":"बहूनां पुरुषाणां स यथैका योनिरुच्यते ।\nतथा तं पुरुषं विश्वं परमं सुमहत्तमम् ।\nनिर्गुणं निर्गुणा भूत्वा प्रविशन्ति सनातनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"As one source is spoken of for many persons, so that Person, the universe, supreme and greatest, is the eternal one without qualities; those without qualities, becoming qualityless, enter him."}}]}]}